  "design": {
    "repeatedWork": "Cached ordinary narrow byte row privately divides8quotients, constructs fixed margins, checks half boundaries, clips/rounds and packs. Bounded and cached-wide execution already share TryWriteOrdinaryBytePair.",
    "endState": "Replace duplicate ordinary cached-byte publisher with existing certified common helper and unchanged Original repair. Keep ordered filter/preparation/workspace untouched. No new coefficient layout, owner, pool, session or numerical policy.",
    "temporaryCosts": "Reciprocal/Newton certificate replaces full division but uses alphaSum>=16 and normalized-alpha guard, possibly increasing original-order replay for low alpha. Common helper may affect caller JIT/inlining. Count source-level changes only as hypotheses; use complete operations. Preserve adverse results.",
    "numericalScope": "Only ordinary byte cached rows with capacity16; TryPrepare bounds tapsX/tapsY<=16. Same ordered double sums and existing400/2^40 error bound, normalizer>=.5/alphaSum>=16, critical quotient257/reciprocal error<2^-27, margin2^-16; unchanged exact original-order/tiny-alpha repair. No pixel policy change.",
    "ownership": "TryApply/plan Execute use unpublished independently owned result and admitted caller/operation workspace; on failure enclosing public owner cleans up. Shared helper false leaves destination unchanged. No new storage, scope, reservation, pool or retention.",
    "reuse": "Other Cached row methods, geometry/preparation/working ownership and word/bounded helpers are verbatim."
  },
